Hi,

My i840-based Supermicro PIIIDME (single Coppermine
PIII 933 MHz with SMP kernel) was able to boot with
"acpi=force" when I used Linux 2.4.22. (2.4.22 had a
nasty oops on shutdown, but...). However, when I tried
booting with ACPI on 2.4.23 I discovered that my PCI
devices started misbehaving. My Ethernet and AGP
devices refused to enable, for example. I have managed
to boot using the "pci=noacpi" option, and everything
seems OK at the moment.

I have attached two logs. The first is a sucessful
ACPI boot from 2.4.22 (made in the days before one of
my CPU-slots failed), the second is my boot-logs from
2.4.23 (both with and without pci=noacpi).

Cheers,
Chris


